      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "As Electron is combination of chromium + node, N-API native module can be used in browser(Blink) process. It can [create an external ArrayBuffer](https://nodejs.org/api/n-api.html#n_api_napi_create_external_arraybuffer)\r\nThe problem is, [Blink does not allow external ArrayBuffer expect externalized one by Blink](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src.git/+/master/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/templates/interface.cc.tmpl#1027).\r\nIn result, when external ArrayBuffer created by N-API is passed to Blink, such as `WebGLContext.texImage2D(ArrayBufferView)`, chromium crashes.\r\nI don't know the exact reason why Blink does this but maybe kind of keeping it secure.\r\nBut Electron already unleashed sandbox of Blink and allowing external ArrayBuffer to be used would be not a big problem I think.\r\nI can patch it If it can be consented.\r\n",
